WEBVTT

00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:12,070
What do you think of reverse osmosis water?

00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:19,070
Well, personally, we have reverse osmosis water at our clinic.

00:00:19,070 --> 00:00:23,070
Our clinic is out in the country, but we have a lot of nitrates in the water,

00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:27,070
so we do get a reverse osmosis unit because that will take those out.

00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:31,070
At my home, we live in the country, and we have a well also.

00:00:31,070 --> 00:00:36,070
We do not have a reverse osmosis unit because we haven't had our water tested,

00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:40,070
and it's like, great. So I want the nutrients that are in the water too,

00:00:40,070 --> 00:00:42,070
so I don't have a reverse osmosis.

00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:46,070
But if I every time I didn't live in the city where we had chlorade and fluoride,

00:00:46,070 --> 00:00:48,070
we had a reverse osmosis unit.

00:00:48,070 --> 00:00:52,070
A lot of people say, oh, that's not good because you know your water's dead.

00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:57,070
I'm sorry, but you know, I'm not drinking my water to get minerals from my water.

00:00:57,070 --> 00:00:59,070
I'm drinking my water for the water.

00:00:59,070 --> 00:01:02,070
So I'm getting minerals for my food.

00:01:02,070 --> 00:01:04,070
So I don't buy that argument.

00:01:04,070 --> 00:01:12,070
I think reverse osmosis is the best way to take out, you know, other things and chemicals that, you know,

00:01:12,070 --> 00:01:15,070
and just a simple carbon filter won't take out.

00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:19,070
Carbon will take out a lot of the fluoride and a lot of the chlorine,

00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:21,070
but it's not going to take out the nitrates.

00:01:21,070 --> 00:01:29,070
It's not going to take out any like heavy metals or mercury or arsenic and things that are commonly in water.

00:01:29,070 --> 00:01:32,070
So I am a fan of reverse osmosis.

